# axiom explain, every code and every spelling.
# AX1001-AX5001 were materialized from the Rust compiler at commit 1041f11 on
# 2026-08-08; AX3018 and above (macros, visibility, limits, traits, effects, the
# FFI boundary, type soundness) postdate it and originate in self_host/explain.ax. The list COLOUR is RECONSTRUCTED, not captured. AX2004 was REWRITTEN on 2026-08-18 when the `extern` FFI landed: its captured text said generated code links no C library, which stopped being true for a program that binds a std Rust crate. AX3010 was REWRITTEN on 2026-08-25 when it was PROMOTED from a warning to an ERROR: its captured text described a mismatch an agent could correct at leisure, and it now refuses the build. Those two are the only codes in the AX1001-AX5001 range that are no longer the 2026-08-08 bytes.
